                <pb facs="0563" n="483" sameAs="frus:frus1930v01/pg483"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">832.12/23</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Ambassador in
                        Brazil</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Morgan</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1930-08-30">August 30, 1930</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1562</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: The Department has received your despatch
                    No. 3387 dated July 23, 1930, concerning the cases of persons of both American
                    and Brazilian nationalities who desire to have their American passports visaed
                    to enable them to leave Brazil.</p>
                <p>You are informed that the American consular officers in Brazil are being
                    instructed to take up all such cases with the Embassy in the future instead of
                    taking them up with the local police authorities.</p>
                <p>Very truly yours.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">W. R. Castle, Jr.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
